# OWNER REVIEW
# Vesper in Primrose Close: her lesson at the Neighbourhood Watch hut (Fetch and Open, in the suit;
# levels/primrose/keys/vesper_lesson.gd), and her night on the steeple (Key 4; levels/primrose/keys/steeple.gd).

~ lesson_garb
Vesper [calm]: Not in that. This lesson's for the suit.
Vesper: Number 4 has a wardrobe in its porch. I'll wait.

~ lesson_watch
Vesper [calm]: The Neighbourhood Watch. They'll do anything for someone who sounds as if she's in charge.
Vesper: Watch me ask him for the hut's key.
Vesper: Fetch me the hut key, please.

~ lesson_open
Vesper: Thank you. And the door.
Vesper: Open the hut for me.

~ lesson_teach
Vesper [warm]: Fetch, and Open. Asked, not barked. He wants to be useful. Let him.
Vesper: Ask more of someone than they can give, and it costs you. Know who you're asking.
Vesper: Your turn. His thermos, and the postbox.

~ lesson_turn
Vesper [calm]: The thermos, then the postbox. Fetch, then Open. I'm watching.

~ lesson_done
[narrator] Inside the postbox: forty party invitations on cream card. Every one is addressed to a councillor.
Vesper [calm]: Forty. One street. Every one to someone with a vote.
Vesper [warm]: Good. You asked as if you meant it, and you thanked him. Both matter.
Vesper: I'll be on the steeple. I can see the whole Close from there.

~ mind_the_bells
Vesper [calm]: Mind the bells.
Nim: What about the...

~ after_bells
Nim: ...Ow.
Vesper [warm]: I did say.

~ belfry
Vesper [calm]: Every net curtain on the street, from up here. Every light that's on, and every one that went off when the van came.
- Come down and help? => help
- Aren't you cold? => cold

~ help
Vesper [warm]: You don't need me down there. You're already doing what I'd do.

~ cold
Vesper: Yes. Someone has to watch anyway.

~ garden_after
Vesper [calm]: Forty parties, every one in a councillor's house. It was never about the toys. It was about who was holding them.
Vesper: And the Docks, next. Get some sleep first.
